### TypeScript style in this repo

- Prefer explicit function and exported API types; avoid `any` unless interop or mocking requires it.
- Use meaningful names (no 1–2 character identifiers) and keep code readable (prefer multi-line over dense one-liners).
- Use early returns to simplify control flow and handle errors up front.
- Keep comments minimal and focused on intent, not mechanics.
- Match existing formatting; do not reformat unrelated code in edits.
